1
00:00:02,963 --> 00:00:05,803
(Sheldon:)I have a question
about Batman.

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:09,940
(Sheldon:)Batman is a man
who dresses up like a bat.

3
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:14,310
(Sheldon:)Man-bat is a part man,
part bat hybrid.

4
00:00:14,311 --> 00:00:15,741
(Sheldon:)Now,

5
00:00:15,745 --> 00:00:19,045
(Sheldon:)if Man-Bat dressed up as a man
to fight crime,

6
00:00:19,049 --> 00:00:22,379
(Sheldon:)would he be Man-Batman?

7
00:00:22,385 --> 00:00:25,485
(Leonard:)No, he'd be Bat-Man-Bat.

8
00:00:26,523 --> 00:00:28,893
(Raj:)But wouldn't Man-Batman
just be a Batman

9
00:00:28,892 --> 00:00:31,522
(Raj:)that was bitten by
a radioactive man?

10
00:00:31,528 --> 00:00:33,498
(Howard:)But Batman is a man.

11
00:00:33,497 --> 00:00:36,527
(Howard:)You're talking about a man who
would have the powers of a man.

12
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:39,533
(Howard:)That's just Man-Man.

13
00:00:39,536 --> 00:00:41,366
(Sheldon:)Well, isn't Man-Man just Man?

14
00:00:41,371 --> 00:00:43,341
(Leonard:)But what if Man-Man
dressed as a bat?

15
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:44,240
(Raj:)Well, that's just Batman.

16
00:00:44,241 --> 00:00:46,271
(Leonard:)No, if a man dresses as a bat,

17
00:00:46,276 --> 00:00:48,446
(Leonard:)that's Batman,
but if Man-Man dresses as a bat,

18
00:00:48,445 --> 00:00:50,245
(Leonard:)that's Batman-Man.

19
00:00:50,247 --> 00:00:51,817
(cell phone chimes)

20
00:00:51,815 --> 00:00:53,345
(Howard:)So does that answer
your question?

21
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:56,050
(Sheldon:)Oh, I haven't asked it yet.

22
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:58,420
(Raj(checking text on phone):)Oh, that's Claire.
Got to run.

23
00:00:58,421 --> 00:01:00,451
(Leonard:)I thought you were back
with Emily.

24
00:01:00,457 --> 00:01:03,157
(Raj:)Uh, actually I'm...
seeing both of them.

25
00:01:03,159 --> 00:01:06,859
(Leonard:)You mean like through their
window from behind a bush?

26
00:01:08,331 --> 00:01:11,201
(Raj:)No, I'm actually dating
two women.

27
00:01:11,201 --> 00:01:13,901
(Raj:)Later.

28
00:01:13,904 --> 00:01:15,734
(chuckles)
Really?

29
00:01:15,739 --> 00:01:18,069
(Leonard:)The guy who for years
couldn't even talk to women

30
00:01:18,074 --> 00:01:19,704
(Leonard:)is suddenly going out
with two of them?

31
00:01:19,709 --> 00:01:21,579
(Leonard:)How is that possible?
WOLOWITZ: I know.

32
00:01:21,578 --> 00:01:23,048
(Howard:)Scientists have tried
to reproduce it

33
00:01:23,046 --> 00:01:24,276
(Howard:)with computational models,

34
00:01:24,281 --> 00:01:27,411
(Howard:)but, in each case,
the world blows up.

35
00:01:32,656 --> 00:01:34,956
(Leonard:)Seriously, that guy's
dating two women?

36
00:01:36,092 --> 00:01:39,732
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

